msgid "00_planb_testsite/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "00_planb_testsite/name"
msgstr "Training Area"

msgid "01_karelia/description"
msgstr ""
"Swamps, rocks and cliffs determine major avenues of approach on this map. "
"This map, with sparse protection and no buildings, gives the combat "
"advantage to artillery. Concentrate your attacks along the path of your main"
" advance, while conducting delaying and defensive actions along the rest of "
"your front lines."

msgid "01_karelia/name"
msgstr "Karelia"

msgid "02_malinovka/description"
msgstr ""
"Initial staging areas are separated by a wide open field, ideal for "
"artillery and defensive operations. Make use of flanking maneuvers and "
"natural defenses like woods, hills and farmhouses, as these can be decisive."
" Another option is a well-coordinated high-speed combined arms attack across"
" the field, which could bring victory at the risk of a bloody loss."

msgid "02_malinovka/name"
msgstr "Malinovka"

msgid "02_malinovka_4CT_mode/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "02_malinovka_4CT_mode/name"
msgstr "Malinovka 4 Bases"

msgid "03_campania/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "03_campania/name"
msgstr "Campania"

msgid "04_himmelsdorf/description"
msgstr ""
"A labyrinth of streets and squares, impassable for artillery and tank "
"destroyers, but ideal for speedy breakthrough and bypass by medium and light"
" vehicles. Access roads running by the hill, with the castle that dominates "
"the area, and along the railway lines can help you out of the impasse."

msgid "04_himmelsdorf/name"
msgstr "Himmelsdorf"

msgid "05_prohorovka/description"
msgstr ""
"Generally open, but hilly terrain around a vital railroad, with groups of "
"trees providing shelter for tank destroyers. On the offensive, watch your "
"own flanks while striking against the enemy flanks. Artillery has free "
"reign, although it is still vulnerable to raids by light vehicles."

msgid "05_prohorovka/name"
msgstr "Prokhorovka"

msgid "06_ensk/description"
msgstr ""
"A mixture of city outskirts and suburban areas, bisected by railroad tracks."
" Plan your tactics to take advantage of defensive choke points and cover "
"open areas with your vehicles. Artillery is great for deterring enemy "
"breakthroughs, but remains almost defenseless when exposed to enemy vehicles"
" attacking from cover."

msgid "06_ensk/name"
msgstr "Ensk"

msgid "07_lakeville/description"
msgstr ""
"An isolated mountain valley on one flank and city blocks on the other allow "
"you to thrust close enough to the enemy. A large lake in the middle gives "
"long-range weapons a clear field of fire."

msgid "07_lakeville/name"
msgstr "Lakeville"

msgid "08_ruinberg/description"
msgstr ""
"Concentric city streets, along with dense forests and bushes in the "
"overgrown park allow for hidden maneuvers and redeployment of your troops. "
"Although artillery fire is of limited use in the city, the debris provides "
"effective cover for your troops."

msgid "08_ruinberg/name"
msgstr "Ruinberg"

msgid "10_hills/description"
msgstr ""
"A high hill in the center of the map provides a perfect outpost for your "
"attacks. A village to the north-east of the hill and an island to the west "
"offer a wide range of tactic advantages, but lay open to fire from the "
"center."

msgid "10_hills/name"
msgstr "Mines"

msgid "11_murovanka/description"
msgstr ""
"Swamps, ravines and hills determine your battle tactics. The scarcity of "
"buildings gives a combat advantage to artillery. Concentrating all your "
"attacks along one axis of attack may prove the best strategy."

msgid "11_murovanka/name"
msgstr "Murovanka"

msgid "12_scorched_earth/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "12_scorched_earth/name"
msgstr "Scorched Earth"

msgid "13_erlenberg/description"
msgstr ""
"Divided by a river, this map offers three main avenues of attack. A bridge "
"in the center is situated among the ruins of a small town. Terrain around "
"the northern and southern bridges offers a small amount of cover. Use the "
"castle and the range of hills on the opposite side of the map as firing "
"positions for your artillery."

msgid "13_erlenberg/name"
msgstr "Erlenberg"

msgid "13_erlenberg_winter/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "13_erlenberg_winter/name"
msgstr "Happy New Year Erlenberg!"

msgid "14_siegfried_line/description"
msgstr ""
"The map is a combination of open spaces and city blocks. Meandering lanes "
"will facilitate your surprise attacks from behind the enemy lines while "
"numerous bunkers serve as cover."

msgid "14_siegfried_line/name"
msgstr "Siegfried Line"

msgid "15_komarin/description"
msgstr ""
"This map starts both teams away from their bases, providing for a variety of"
" tactical decision making. Both teams face a tough choice—whether to roll "
"out to defend their bases or attempt to capture the enemy base. It is up to "
"you to decide, as either tactic may lead your team to victory or failure."

msgid "15_komarin/name"
msgstr "Komarin"

msgid "17_munchen/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "17_munchen/name"
msgstr "Munich"

msgid "18_cliff/description"
msgstr ""
"Opposing bases on this map are separated by cliffs and rocky ridges. A "
"variety of cover allows for focused attacks in crucial directions. The "
"center may seem ideal for breakthrough operations but do not neglect your "
"flanks!"

msgid "18_cliff/name"
msgstr "Cliff"

msgid "19_monastery/description"
msgstr ""
"A monastery and a town are the focal points of this map. Three roads run "
"from north to south providing easy access from one end of the map to the "
"other. The monastery courtyard offers perfect, but predictable, firing "
"positions for your tanks and artillery. The long hill in the west and the "
"winding ravine in the east can serve as perfect cover from enemy fire."

msgid "19_monastery/name"
msgstr "Abbey"

msgid "22_slough/description"
msgstr ""
"Flank passageways offer great opportunities for surprise attacks and "
"diversionary operations. A mire in the center is not a mere obstacle, but an"
" important tactical location."

msgid "22_slough/name"
msgstr "Swamp"

msgid "23_westfeld/description"
msgstr ""
"Lush terrain with forests and villages scattered throughout the map and a "
"gigantic crumbling aqueduct to the east of the valley. A variety of cliffs "
"and ridges allow for perfect ambush spots, but wide open areas make changing"
" your position quite risky."

msgid "23_westfeld/name"
msgstr "Westfield"

msgid "24_canyon/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "24_canyon/name"
msgstr "zFrozen Canyon"

msgid "26_river_valley/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "26_river_valley/name"
msgstr "zFrozen River Vale"

msgid "27_ardennes/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "27_ardennes/name"
msgstr "Ardennes"

msgid "28_desert/description"
msgstr ""
"This map looks open, but appearances can be deceiving! The village houses "
"can be used as cover for vehicles and artillery. Consider attacking on the "
"enemy flanks safely protected from their fire by cliffs and dunes."

msgid "28_desert/name"
msgstr "Sand River"

msgid "29_el_hallouf/description"
msgstr ""
"A spacious valley sprinkled with boulders and trees lies in the center of "
"the map. High mountain ridges flanking the valley provide a variety of "
"sniper positions. Capturing bases becomes a real feat, as both team bases "
"are situated in easily-defended hilly regions."

msgid "29_el_hallouf/name"
msgstr "El Halluf"

msgid "30_africa_airfield/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "30_africa_airfield/name"
msgstr "zFrozen Airfield"

msgid "31_airfield/description"
msgstr ""
"This map is abundant in perfect ambush spots and possibilities for maneuvers"
" and breakthroughs. A large airfield in the upper part of the map and a "
"rocky highland in the center offer a major tactical challenge. Occupy the "
"highland to get perfect view of surrounding terrain and routes to the enemy "
"base."

msgid "31_airfield/name"
msgstr "Airfield"

msgid "33_fjord/description"
msgstr ""
"Huge mountains and narrow valleys offer great advantages in a battle. You "
"can engage in a fire duel across the gulf or enter a close quarter battle at"
" the nearest port town or flank and capture enemy base."

msgid "33_fjord/name"
msgstr "Fjords"

msgid "34_redshire/description"
msgstr ""
"This map is truly exceptional. Fields passing smoothly into hills offer "
"great opportunities for aggressive attacks. The river crossing the map in "
"the middle is rather a remarkable guiding landmark than an obstacle."

msgid "34_redshire/name"
msgstr "Redshire"

msgid "35_steppes/description"
msgstr ""
"Generally open, this map allows you to disperse your forces in various "
"directions, but don't leave them too weak. A road in the center will take "
"you to the enemy base more quickly, but perhaps with greater difficulty. "
"This map is ideal for flank attacks and feints."

msgid "35_steppes/name"
msgstr "Steppes"

msgid "36_fishing_bay/description"
msgstr ""
"The map is a combination of open spaces and irregular terrain. Meandering "
"narrow streets of the seaport on the flank can be surprisingly advantageous."
" Sloping hills covered with bushes offer excellent ambush opportunities."

msgid "36_fishing_bay/name"
msgstr "Fisherman's Bay"

msgid "37_caucasus/description"
msgstr ""
"Use the rough terrain of the map to hide from enemy fire, organize ambush "
"operations, or find your way to the enemy base unnoticed through winding "
"highland paths."

msgid "37_caucasus/name"
msgstr "Mountain Pass"

msgid "38_mannerheim_line/description"
msgstr ""
"This snow-covered and rocky map is abundant in various obstacles and "
"defilades. Meandering passageways around rocky mountains and along the "
"river-side will facilitate your surprise attacks from behind the enemy lines"
" and will offer plenty of ambush opportunities."

msgid "38_mannerheim_line/name"
msgstr "Arctic Region"

msgid "39_crimea/description"
msgstr "?empty?"

msgid "39_crimea/name"
msgstr "Foros"

